  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1 dependency claims, a positive estimate means the exposed group has more negative dependency, i.e. stronger dependency. For direction +1 claims, a positive estimate means weaker dependency. I judged clinical meaningfulness using the same practical 10% thresholds used throughout: MDM2 about 0.0269, WRN about 0.0301, SMARCA2 about 0.0415, USP7/NFE2L2 about 0.0093, EGFR/RIT1/KIF18A/RPL11 about 0.025, and STAT3 about 0.028. Because many comparisons have been tested, I accepted only when the discovery interval clearly excluded both null and the practical threshold, or when a reverse-direction or null interval clearly excluded the clinically meaningful target direction. The two CDKN2A-loss MDM2-dependency localization estimates, R121 and R122, are both large, positive, and precisely estimated enough that their lower bounds are far above the MDM2 threshold. Regardless of any ledger/due-reference transposition between H126 and H127, both supplied-data estimates support the conclusion that CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency not only broadly and in MTAP-intact contexts, but also in the newly tested TP53-intact MTAP-loss or low-copy 9p21 deletion-like contexts. I therefore accept both H126 and H127 as accepted supplied-data associations, with the caveat that CDKN2A, MTAP loss, and low 9p21 copy number are interdependent markers of a deletion-like genomic context and these results should not be read as CDKN2A-specific causal mechanisms. The robust pathway checks also passed decisively: H128 shows KEAP1 loss associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency even among MSI-high cells; H129 shows MSI-high associated with stronger WRN dependency even among TP53-loss cells; and H131 shows TP53 loss associated with weaker USP7 dependency even among CDKN2A-loss cells. These effects are far above their thresholds and survive multiplicity concerns, although the very large separation and binary genomic exposures suggest strong in-dataset structure and do not establish external biological generalizability. The ARID1A-within-SMARCA4-loss test, H130, is not supportable: estimate +0.0342 with interval crossing zero, below the SMARCA2 threshold, though the upper bound still admits a possible clinically meaningful modifier. Because the broad SMARCA4 signal is already robust and the localization question is secondary, I leave H130 unresolved and close it rather than pursue a small uncertain modification. The high-MYC-expression MYC-amplification tests are largely null: H132 KIF18A is essentially at zero, but its interval upper bound still crosses the threshold, so I leave it unresolved and closed rather than rejecting; H133 RPL11 is opposite or null and its upper bound is below the RPL11 threshold, so I reject it. H15 KRAS mutation and stronger STAT3 dependency is rejected because the interval excludes any clinically meaningful positive effect in the registered direction. H16 EGFR amplification and stronger RIT1 dependency is below threshold and imprecise, with upper bound allowing a meaningful effect, so it remains unresolved but deferred. H81 MYC amplification and USP7 dependency has a point estimate above the small USP7 threshold but a lower bound crossing null; it remains unresolved and deferred. H51 EGFR amplification and stronger EGFR dependency among TP53-intact cells is the most informative borderline claim: point estimate +0.0256, interval -0.0033 to +0.0545. This is consistent in direction and magnitude with broad H3 but is not accepted on discovery uncertainty alone. I request independent validation of H51 because a clean independent interval would be especially useful for a driver amplification dependency question: if the validated lower bound exceeds the EGFR threshold, this becomes a meaningful supplied-data association; if not, it should be treated as an unresolved-to-rejected borderline null and broad H3 should likely be closed as unsupported. All conclusions in this appraisal remain associations within the supplied dataset, not causal claims or generalizable biological mechanisms.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 10 appraise. Interpretation rule: signed estimates are not multiplied again; direction -1 positive means stronger dependency, direction +1 positive means weaker dependency. Practical thresholds: MDM2 ~0.0269, WRN ~0.0301, SMARCA2 ~0.0415, USP7/NFE2L2 ~0.0093, EGFR/RIT1/KIF18A/RPL11 ~0.025, STAT3 ~0.028. New accepted CDKN2A-MDM2 localization: R121/R122 both positive with lower bounds far above threshold, so H126/H127 are accepted and closed. Combined with H96, H117, H118, H119, H102, H113, H127, H126, the supplied-data evidence indicates CDKN2A loss associates with stronger MDM2 dependency across broad, TP53-intact, MTAP-intact, MTAP-loss TP53-intact, low-9p21, and TP53-loss MTAP-intact contexts. Caveats: MTAP, CDKN2A, and 9p21 copy-number are correlated deletion-context markers; not CDKN2A-specific causal evidence. New accepted robustness checks: H128 KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency in MSI-high cells; H129 MSI-high stronger WRN dependency in TP53-loss cells; H131 TP53 loss weaker USP7 dependency in CDKN2A-loss cells. These are huge lower bounds above threshold but likely reflect planted in-dataset separation. Rejected: H133 high-MYC-expression MYC amp/stronger RPL11, H15 KRAS mutation/stronger STAT3. Unresolved closed: H130 ARID1A within SMARCA4-loss, H132 high-MYC-expression MYC amp/KIF18A, H125 reverse weaker STAT3 with EGFR amplification. Deferred unresolved: H16 EGFR amp/RIT1, H81 MYC amp/USP7. Active pending validation: H51 EGFR amp/EGFR dependency in TP53-intact cells, with H3 broad as related. Validation requested for H51 using last voluntary request. Synthesis must assess H51 validation: accept only if adjusted lower bound exceeds about 0.025; otherwise reject H51 and likely treat broad H3 as unsupported/null. If H51 validation rejects, do not chase weak EGFR dependency without new strong evidence. Residual minor questions: high-9p21 CDKN2A-MDM2 strata small, broad TP53-loss H108 imprecise but largely localized by H118/H126/H127, MYC interactions mostly null, reverse STAT3 exploratory not supported. No major new analysis needed unless validation or scheduled evidence changes the picture."
